<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">3</span>Think and discuss</h2><ol class="ws-qs"><li><p><b>Clovis culture</b>. Its profile says: &#8220;Clovis is the earliest widely recognised archaeological culture of North America, found from southern Canada to northern Mexico around 13,050 to 12,750 years ago.&#8221; Find one piece of evidence on the profile for this, and say how we know it.</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p><b>Caral–Supe civilisation</b>. Its profile says: &#8220;Caral–Supe was a cluster of as many as thirty population centres in three small valleys of Peru’s north-central coast, flourishing between about 3000 and 1800 BCE.&#8221; Find one piece of evidence on the profile for this, and say how we know it.</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p><b>Maya civilisation</b>. Its profile says: &#8220;From the 1st millennium BCE to the Spanish conquest, the Maya of southern Mexico and Central America built hundreds of cities, from El Mirador and Tikal to Chichén Itzá, but never a single state.&#8221; Find one piece of evidence on the profile for this, and say how we know it.</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p>Choose two of these cultures that lived at the same time. What did they have in common, and what set them apart?</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li></ol></section>
<p class="ws-src">From The Epoch Institute: the-epoch-institute.org/profiles?kind=culture&amp;region=Americas. Free to print and copy for use in class.</p>
<details class="ws-key" id="answers"><summary>Answer key</summary><div class="ws-key-b"><p class="ws-key-t">Answer key: Worksheet: Cultures of the Americas</p><section><h2><span class="ws-n">1</span>Put the cultures in order</h2><ol class="ws-key-list"><li>Clovis culture <span>c. 11100 BCE – c. 10800 BCE</span></li><li>Caral–Supe civilisation <span>c. 3000 BCE – c. 1800 BCE</span></li><li>Maya civilisation <span>c. 2000 BCE – 1697 CE</span></li><li>Ancestral Puebloans <span>c. 1500 BCE – c. 1600 CE</span></li><li>Olmecs <span>c. 1200 BCE – c. 400 BCE</span></li><li>Paracas culture <span>c. 800 BCE – c. 100 BCE</span></li><li>Mapuche <span>c. 500 BCE to today</span></li></ol></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">2</span>Match the cultures to their homelands</h2><ol class="ws-key-list" type="A"><li>Clovis culture <span>4: Across North America, from southern Canada to northern Mexico and across the east and west of the continent</span></li><li>Caral–Supe civilisation <span>5: The Supe, Pativilca and Fortaleza valleys of north-central coastal Peru, 150–200 km north of Lima, with…</span></li><li>Maya civilisation <span>2: The Yucatán Peninsula and the lands to its south</span></li><li>Ancestral Puebloans <span>1: The Colorado Plateau around the Four Corners of the south-western United States, where Arizona, New Mexico,…</span></li><li>Olmecs <span>6: The tropical lowlands of the Gulf of Mexico in southern Veracruz and western Tabasco, Mexico, with…</span></li><li>Paracas culture <span>3: The south coast of Peru, in today’s Ica Region</span></li></ol></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">3</span>Think and discuss</h2><p class="ws-key-note">Open questions: answers will vary. Good answers use details from the profiles.</p></section></div></details>
